# Environment variables — Hospedajes Valle

Copy to `.env.local` and fill in when connecting Supabase.

```bash
# Public site URL (production domain — used for Open Graph link previews)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.tudominio.com

# Data source: "static" (default) | "supabase"
NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_PROVIDER=static

# Supabase project (required when DATA_PROVIDER=supabase)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only — never expose to the browser (Route Handlers, migrations, webhooks)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Storage bucket for property gallery images
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PROPERTY_IMAGES_BUCKET=property-images

# Pre-reservation email notifications (Resend — https://resend.com)
RESEND_API_KEY=
PRE_RESERVATION_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# Optional — use your verified domain in production (e.g. reservas@hospedajesvalle.com)
PRE_RESERVATION_FROM_EMAIL=Hospedajes Valle <onboarding@resend.dev>
```

## Quick start (Supabase)

1. Create a Supabase project.
2. Run `supabase/schema.sql` in the SQL Editor.
3. Create Storage bucket `property-images` (public read, auth write).
4. Copy project URL + anon key to `.env.local`.
5. Install deps: `npm install @supabase/supabase-js @supabase/ssr`
6. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_PROVIDER=supabase`.
7. Implement stubs in `lib/supabase/queries/` and swap dashboard store to Supabase.

See `docs/BACKEND.md` for the full integration checklist.
